==Trivia==
*The word "''Golem''" occurs once in the Bible in Psalm 139:16, which uses the word "''golmi''", that means "my light form", "raw" material, connoting the unfinished human being. A golem is an animated, anthropomorphic being in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jewish_folklore Jewish folklore], which is entirely created from inanimate matter, usually clay or mud. The most famous golem narrative involves [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judah_Loew_ben_Bezalel Judah Loew ben Bezalel], the late 16th-century rabbi of Prague.
**In the Vietnamese language setting of the game, the Golem's name translates to "Stone Man".
*The Golem was likely inspired by the [https://ageofempires.fandom.com/wiki/Promethean Promethean] from [https://ageofempires.fandom.com/wiki/Age_of_Mythology Age of Mythology], as both units are stone creatures that split in two, smaller versions of themselves once defeated.
*The Golem is 1 of 19 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] which first existed in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Minions]], [[Archers]], [[Goblins]], [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Balloon]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Phoenix]], [[Lava Hound]], and the [[Archer Queen]].
**The Golem resembles the Level 6 Golem from Clash of Clans.
**The Golem in Clash Royale shares its deploy sound effect with its Clash of Clans counterpart's.
**In Clash Royale, Golemites possess a unique design, animations, and sound effects, while in Clash of Clans, Golemites are a scaled-down version of the Golem, and have the same sound effects as the Golem, only at a higher pitch.
**Unlike in Clash of Clans, the Clash Royale counterpart always spawns 2 Golemites regardless of Level, while the Golem in Clash of Clans may spawn more than 2 Golemites depending on the Level.
*It is the most expensive {{Rarity|Epic}} [[Cards|card]], costing 8 [[Elixir]], not counting the [[Mirror]] as it does not have a [[:Category:Variable-Elixir Cards|defined Elixir cost]].
**It is also currently the only permanent 8 Elixir card in Clash Royale.
*The Golem's stats are the highest or lowest among all troops. More specifically:
**The Golem has the highest hitpoints of all troops, with 7,456 hitpoints at Level 15.
**The Golem has the longest deployment time of all troops, with a deployment time of 3 seconds.
*The Golem has been featured in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special game modes]] outside of the card. More specifically:
**The Golem is 1 of 23 troops that have been featured in the [[Troop Rush]] game [[:Category:Modes|mode]], the others being Skeletons, [[Skeleton Dragons]], [[Fire Spirit]], [[Bats]], [[Elite Barbarians]], [[Firecracker]], [[Rascals|Rascal Girls]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Heal Spirit]], [[Elixir Golem]], [[Guards]], [[Prince]], Balloon, Wall Breakers, [[Ram Rider]], [[Sparky]], Phoenix, [[Royal Ghost]], [[Bandit]], [[Lumberjack]], [[Santa Hog Rider]], and the [[Monk]].
**The Golem is 1 of 10 troops that has been featured under the [[Ruler Ability#Special Delivery|Special Delivery]] [[Ruler Ability|ruler ability]], the others being [[Knight]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Musketeer]], Wizard, P.E.K.K.A, [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Sparky]], and Royal Ghost.
*The Golem shares the first part of his description with the Giant.
*The Golem is 1 of 15 troops which bring an excited reaction from the audience upon spawning and brings a collective groan from the audience when defeated, as well as a concerning gasp when the opponent plays it, the others include [[Royal Giant]], Giant, P.E.K.K.A, Giant Skeleton, [[Rune Giant]], [[Goblin Giant]], Bowler, [[Electro Wizard]], [[Inferno Dragon]], Sparky, Lava Hound, [[Night Witch]], [[Super Lava Hound]], and the Monk.
*A [[Loading Screen Hints|Loading Screen Hint]] suggests that the Golem's heart is made of stone.
*Unlike the Ice Golem, the Golem only punches with one hand, whereas the [[Ice Golem]] attacks with both hands. The Elixir Golem attacks with both hands, but the Elixir Golemites use one hand and the Elixir Blobs appear to bite.
*The Golem is featured as a [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Hero_Skins?file=Golem_King_info.png skin for Barbarian King in Clash of Clans].
*The Golem is featured in non-Clash games. More specifically:
**The Golem, along with the Goblins and the Archer Queen, was featured as a character skin for the Rook in [https://www.chess.com/ Chess].
**The Golem, along with the Minions, [[Bomber]], Skeletons, Skeleton Dragons, [[Ice Spirit]], Mini P.E.K.K.A, [[Mega Minion]], Ice Golem, [[Dart Goblin]], Elixir Golem, [[Goblin Cage|Goblin Brawler]], Guards, [[Baby Dragon]], P.E.K.K.A, Giant Skeleton, Wall Breakers, Bowler, [[Executioner]], [[Mega Knight]], Inferno Dragon, Royal Ghost, and Lava Hound, are featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Monsters monster] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
***A [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Gem_Golem gem variant] for the Golem is also featured as a monster in Squad Buster.
*The Golem is the subject of 4 [[Emotes]].
*The Golem was featured in the winning [[Battle Decks|deck]] of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/1fuCnNBTqBU?feature=share King's Cup Tournament], by a player called TMD YAOYAO.
*Before the Golem's card release, the Golem's and its Golemites' hitpoints were decreased by 4%.

